<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Real Audiencia of Quito</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1563">1563</a>–<a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Presidency of Quito</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Real <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quito">Quito</a> was a Spanish colonial court and administrative unit created in 1563, covering most of present-day Ecuador and parts of southern Colombia and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. It belonged first to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a> and from 1739 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-granada">New Granada</a>. Ecuador later claimed its territory, including vast Amazonian lands, as the basis of its borders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/real-audiencia-of-quito.jpg" alt="Real Audiencia of Quito" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Requena y Herrera · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Real_Audiencia_de_Quito_1779.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
